      "description": "The task stated directly, as a specification rather than a tutorial:\nthe physics, the parameters, and the deliverables, with no\npedagogical scaffolding at all.\nSame physics, parameters and conventions as `guided` (so ground truth\nand grading are unchanged), but there is no worked output schema, no\nexample, no \"give the EXACT result\" instruction, no order-of-magnitude\nwarning, and no convention hints; the system prompt carries no task\nguidance whatsoever, only the autonomy contract. Only the irreducible\ngrading interface survives -- the answer path, the field names, the\nunits and the formula symbol alphabet -- because without it a correct\ncomputation is ungradeable.\n\nThe prompt also asks for `results/derivation.md`, a free-form record of\nhow the answer was reached. It is deliberately UNGRADED (the rubric is\nfamily-level, so all three spec rungs stay reach-comparable); it\nsurvives via the benchmark's artifacts keep_full '.md' rule purely as\npost-hoc evidence for diagnosing error modes.\n\nThe guided -> scaffold_minimal -> unguided ladder is the specification\naxis at full, lean and zero scaffolding.\n",
